Has anyone seen it do anything else?

00:30:00.020 --> 00:30:01.620
That's it. That's the only thing it does.

00:30:01.740 --> 00:30:05.940
Cause the manual says, I wish I had it right here.

00:30:06.200 --> 00:30:11.160
It's basically along the lines of like, it's going to lift you up.

00:30:11.740 --> 00:30:15.940
And if you press the A button, it'll bring you back down to earth.

00:30:16.300 --> 00:30:19.020
Well, what it says is, I'm just reading it now.

00:30:19.020 --> 00:30:21.980
If you, if you land on one of these, something crazy will happen.

00:30:22.480 --> 00:30:25.140
Stay cool and press the A button right on time.

00:30:25.280 --> 00:30:27.900
Like, like, like it's going to be something really stressful and crazy.

00:30:28.040 --> 00:30:30.200
You got to keep your cool and press the A button.

00:30:30.360 --> 00:30:34.240
It's like, that was, that was maybe the most exciting thing that happens in this game.

00:30:34.340 --> 00:30:35.660
And it's not very exciting.

00:30:35.860 --> 00:30:39.820
And the fact that it's not very hard to press the A button on exactly what tile you want.

00:30:39.980 --> 00:30:41.320
There's like no challenge to it.

00:30:41.480 --> 00:30:44.680
One thing I definitely don't think of this game as is stressful.

00:30:45.060 --> 00:30:48.620
I would never describe this like, oh, you shouldn't play this if you have heart problems.

00:30:49.020 --> 00:30:52.840
Yeah. I just love that it says stay cool and press the A button.

00:30:53.040 --> 00:30:54.200
Like, we're here with you.

00:30:54.320 --> 00:30:55.160
You're going to get through this.

00:30:55.340 --> 00:31:00.160
Like, these manual copywriters are doing the best they can with the material they have.

00:31:00.520 --> 00:31:01.500
No, they're definite.

00:31:01.680 --> 00:31:03.300
No, I can't, I can't abide that.

00:31:03.440 --> 00:31:04.640
I don't want to go too off topic.

00:31:04.640 --> 00:31:11.300
But I'd say that most, most manual copywriters actually do a disservice to the games that they're manualizing.

00:31:11.460 --> 00:31:12.400
But this one, though?

00:31:12.980 --> 00:31:18.820
I think this one actually does make it sound, it still doesn't sound exciting, but it sounds more exciting than it actually is.

00:31:19.060 --> 00:31:22.480
I'll grant you anticipation as the exception that proves the rule.

00:31:22.560 --> 00:31:23.820
I thought that's what we were talking about, is anticipation.

00:31:24.040 --> 00:31:25.480
I meant in general.

00:31:25.800 --> 00:31:35.400
Oh, gotcha. So when you win this game at the very end, you get teleported up to what seems like another stage and you're like, oh, great, here we go.

00:31:35.600 --> 00:31:42.920
But then your icon looks at like a trophy of your icon on top of everybody else's icons.

00:31:43.120 --> 00:31:44.680
Like, the other icons have been crushed.

00:31:45.620 --> 00:31:50.580
I mean, I've never won a trophy in my life, but I thought that's how it was.

00:31:51.520 --> 00:31:58.660
Yeah, it's actually, they actually like get 3D models of you and have you stand on all the people on the other baseball team.

00:31:58.860 --> 00:32:04.880
Like, doesn't the Stanley Cup have engravings of the losing team being slaughtered by the winning team?

00:32:04.880 --> 00:32:14.620
No, Sean, it's close, but it's actually that every team that wins the Stanley Cup then just like adds to it of them crushing the previous winners of the Stanley Cup.

00:32:16.600 --> 00:32:17.540
I like that.

00:32:17.740 --> 00:32:20.860
Yeah. So if you don't ever win the Stanley Cup, you never get in that.

00:32:20.920 --> 00:32:21.920
You've never lost, really.

00:32:22.100 --> 00:32:22.900
You've never lost.

00:32:23.200 --> 00:32:26.120
Yeah. So the Buffalo Sabres have nothing to worry about.

00:32:26.380 --> 00:32:28.260
I swear to fucking God.

00:32:28.460 --> 00:32:30.140
I will eat you alive.

00:32:30.320 --> 00:32:33.460
All right. So, I mean, believe it or not, I don't really have much else to talk about here.

00:32:33.460 --> 00:32:42.180
I suppose we could do a rare retrospective, but other than Slalom and Wizards and Warriors, they're pretty much just giving us board games now.

00:32:42.740 --> 00:32:44.840
Oh, sorry. They also gave us RC Pro-Am.

00:32:45.040 --> 00:32:46.660
So they had like three hot.

00:32:46.980 --> 00:32:51.440
Now they've got three that are just like, well, I don't even know if these are really video games at a certain point.

00:32:51.580 --> 00:32:53.060
You know? What is a video game?

00:32:53.740 --> 00:32:57.740
What? RC Pro-Am is like, it's still like a small thing.

00:32:57.880 --> 00:33:00.820
Like they're just trying to remake things that are already in your house.

00:33:01.200 --> 00:33:02.500
Got it. Yeah, that's true.

00:33:02.880 --> 00:33:05.200
RCs are in your house and so are Wizards and Warriors.

00:33:06.780 --> 00:33:10.220
So, you know, I'm not going to, we're not going to do the rare retrospective yet is what I'm saying.

00:33:10.300 --> 00:33:12.800
I think we should wait for them to come out with another big game.

00:33:12.800 --> 00:33:15.780
And then we could kind of ask like, what was the plan?

00:33:15.900 --> 00:33:17.060
Like, why did they go this route?

00:33:17.220 --> 00:33:18.980
I mean, maybe these games made money, right?

00:33:19.060 --> 00:33:25.940
You have to imagine that if you're marketed as the first NES, Nintendo board game, you're probably going to buy that.

00:33:26.080 --> 00:33:27.480
Or your mom's going to buy that for you.

00:33:27.640 --> 00:33:29.860
You know, like your mom's going to be like, oh, board games.

00:33:30.040 --> 00:33:31.420
Great. He's always playing that Nintendo.

00:33:31.440 --> 00:33:33.120
Yeah, I feel like that was more the target.

00:33:33.260 --> 00:33:38.740
It's like parents who really weren't sure what their kids wanted, but they were like, oh, they like board games and they like Nintendo.

00:33:39.060 --> 00:33:44.700
Yeah. And I think we should figure out if we like this in 2020 during our essential games list.

00:33:47.320 --> 00:33:50.240
Joe, you'll notice I said, do we like this game?

00:33:50.720 --> 00:33:53.720
But you're also going to have to give an essential vote.

00:33:54.020 --> 00:33:56.000
So please give both of those.

00:33:56.200 --> 00:33:57.420
So Spy vs.

00:33:57.620 --> 00:33:59.000
Spy, Super Mario Bros.

00:33:59.100 --> 00:34:00.400
3, and Anticipation.

00:34:00.560 --> 00:34:01.800
Those are the last three games we played.

00:34:02.000 --> 00:34:06.460
And I think those are the quintessential, essential games of our time.

00:34:06.580 --> 00:34:07.760
So yes, I'm voting as essential.

00:34:08.840 --> 00:34:13.040
Very good. You'll note that we played Super Mario Bros.

00:34:13.300 --> 00:34:14.280
2, not 3.

00:34:14.500 --> 00:34:17.380
Oh, okay. Well, in that case, that's my mistake.

00:34:17.380 --> 00:34:18.460
So this is not essential.

00:34:18.700 --> 00:34:19.760
Oh, no, no, no, no. Anticipation.

00:34:19.940 --> 00:34:21.020
No, you can't do that.

00:34:21.560 --> 00:34:23.840
No, no. I misunderstood the question.

00:34:24.080 --> 00:34:25.480
I'm going to say not essential.

00:34:26.140 --> 00:34:30.160
I think that they could have done a lot more with this game, even just to make it a play it.

00:34:30.340 --> 00:34:34.580
I think this is just like, like, it's not like it's, it's not like it's some horrible,

00:34:34.700 --> 00:34:37.400
like, it's not like you can't have fun playing this game, but it's just kind of, just kind

00:34:37.400 --> 00:34:41.200
of boring and like not something that you need a video game to do.

00:34:41.460 --> 00:34:44.040
I mean, I guess you need it for the computer to be drawing it.

00:34:44.120 --> 00:34:46.900
But like I said, I already think that's a, that's a mark against it.

00:34:47.020 --> 00:34:50.500
So I think it's just more fun to play this like on paper with a friend.

00:34:50.920 --> 00:34:54.480
Joe, I think you're, yeah, the real trifecta here is,

00:34:54.480 --> 00:34:57.100
uh, Psycross, Suspied vs.

00:34:57.220 --> 00:34:58.340
Spy, Super Mario Bros.

00:34:58.460 --> 00:35:01.480
2, the three S's of October 1988.

00:35:01.760 --> 00:35:04.060
Oh, of course. Yeah, I should have, should have thought of that.

00:35:04.060 --> 00:35:06.200
Yeah, the S tier of games, if you will.

00:35:07.200 --> 00:35:14.440
Now, Sean, you wanted Joe to vote that game essential just now, so I'm scared to hear your

00:35:14.440 --> 00:35:16.460
vote here, but please tell us anyway.

00:35:16.900 --> 00:35:22.560
So I, I, I basically just didn't want him to, uh, to give a joke answer and then go back

00:35:22.560 --> 00:35:25.720
on it. Then I realized that I have done that before many a time.

00:35:25.960 --> 00:35:27.220
So that would be a double standard.

00:35:27.540 --> 00:35:29.440
Yeah, I consider you my inspiration, actually.

00:35:29.640 --> 00:35:30.700
Well, not anymore, but I do.

00:35:31.660 --> 00:35:35.480
Um, so here's, so here's what anticipation is.

00:35:35.880 --> 00:35:41.020
Anticipation is Pictionary, except it removes, uh, it removes you drawing.

00:35:41.300 --> 00:35:46.760
It removes you yelling at your friends the same word over and over, even though they keep

00:35:46.760 --> 00:35:53.140
saying you're wrong. Uh, it, it removes all of the drunken antics that, that would happen alongside that.

00:35:53.260 --> 00:35:57.580
Uh, and it adds a multicolored circle with ice cream on it.

00:35:57.700 --> 00:35:59.880
I would say that this is not essential.

00:35:59.960 --> 00:36:00.940
I think that's well said.

00:36:01.100 --> 00:36:05.360
I, you know, you're, sometimes you forget the human element of it, but even when I was

00:36:05.360 --> 00:36:10.720
playing with another person, I, we never had that moment of shouting out loud, like what

00:36:10.720 --> 00:36:13.180
it is, you know, so that it's missing things like that.

00:36:13.440 --> 00:36:19.200
Yeah. I put anticipation in the category of video games where, uh, you know, a development company

00:36:19.580 --> 00:36:22.140
is told by the publisher, Hey, we need a new game.

00:36:22.140 --> 00:36:25.840
And they just kind of gather around and say, well, we can make this.

00:36:25.980 --> 00:36:27.300
Like we can make this really fast.

00:36:27.420 --> 00:36:28.280
We know how to make this.

00:36:28.400 --> 00:36:29.340
It's easy to make this.

00:36:29.460 --> 00:36:30.340
And then they make it.

00:36:30.420 --> 00:36:32.280
And it's like, it wasn't necessary.

00:36:33.040 --> 00:36:36.740
Anticipation was probably a game that never needed to be made.

00:36:36.740 --> 00:36:39.600
But I understand why it was made back in that time.

00:36:39.780 --> 00:36:44.420
I'm here to tell you right now, you do not need to play it in 2020 and you won't need

00:36:44.420 --> 00:36:47.320
to play it 10 years from now, 20 years from now.

00:36:47.480 --> 00:36:48.320
I guarantee it.

00:36:48.420 --> 00:36:51.620
This game is, is lost to time at this point.

00:36:51.960 --> 00:36:57.720
And we're probably, if it's going to be a rare occasion, if we bring up anticipation

00:36:57.720 --> 00:36:58.800
again on the show.

00:36:59.380 --> 00:37:00.500
Thank you for that, Sean.

00:37:00.500 --> 00:37:07.800
I do have one, I do have one little comment that isn't directly critical of this game.

00:37:08.040 --> 00:37:11.360
And it's just, uh, like the state of the industry, I guess.

00:37:11.460 --> 00:37:15.900
Like, I doubt that they were the first, the first guys to think that like, oh, what if

00:37:15.900 --> 00:37:18.220
we had board game elements in this video game?

00:37:18.340 --> 00:37:24.180
I'm not giving them that credit, but at least shows you where like thoughts of developers

00:37:24.180 --> 00:37:25.540
are headed right now.

00:37:25.540 --> 00:37:31.460
And that like, that there still is that nugget of like, oh, there might be a good board game

00:37:31.460 --> 00:37:37.300
base, like, like in terms of it's, uh, it's, it's gameplay, uh, elements and mechanics.

00:37:37.300 --> 00:37:40.600
Like that could happen over on the horizon maybe.

00:37:40.860 --> 00:37:44.040
So I guess that's, that's all I have to say.

00:37:44.180 --> 00:37:47.740
I think that's a good point though, Sean, that like, we're still trying, you know, people,

00:37:47.960 --> 00:37:52.840
even though the gate, the console is being flooded with games, people are still trying different

00:37:52.840 --> 00:37:55.320
things and seeing what's working in 1988.

00:37:55.600 --> 00:38:00.960
And I'm sure there's going to be a point where we're just going to get continuously hit with

00:38:00.960 --> 00:38:04.100
shmups, sports games, and arcade ports.

00:38:04.340 --> 00:38:09.060
But for the time being, it is nice to have like different stuff just to be able to play

00:38:09.060 --> 00:38:14.800
variety because there was a point in, uh, late 87 where we were almost playing exclusively

00:38:14.800 --> 00:38:22.380
shmups. You know, before we go though, we do have a, you know, a piece of fan mail, if you will,

00:38:22.580 --> 00:38:27.920
a question to, to answer here that's been posed to the nostalgia crew.

00:38:28.240 --> 00:38:29.200
Uh, are you guys game?

00:38:29.340 --> 00:38:30.720
I'm game. Okay.

00:38:31.320 --> 00:38:37.820
Uh, this one comes from Steve from Houston and, uh, he says, best wishes, number one fan.

00:38:38.060 --> 00:38:42.400
I think that's, you know, that's tough to say you're the number one fan, but I believe it

00:38:42.900 --> 00:38:45.920
because it's the first question we've gotten in months.

00:38:46.340 --> 00:38:47.620
And has anyone else said it?

00:38:47.780 --> 00:38:48.840
I mean, you just got to say it.

00:38:48.960 --> 00:38:50.880
Let's not, let's not pit them against each other.

00:38:50.960 --> 00:38:52.760
Yeah. I wouldn't want to pit anybody against each other.

00:38:52.920 --> 00:38:56.020
I think all of our number one fans are exclusively our number one fan.

00:38:56.180 --> 00:39:04.400
I agree. So anyway, the question at hand is if you could remake any game that we've played so far on

00:39:04.400 --> 00:39:11.980
the NES into an open world RPG, which is famously the best genre, what would you pick?

00:39:11.980 --> 00:39:14.120
No cheating with Mario or Link.

00:39:14.340 --> 00:39:16.040
Only hot, fresh IP.

00:39:16.400 --> 00:39:22.280
I got a meeting with Danny Konami and John Bonjaleco to pitch this to tomorrow.

00:39:22.780 --> 00:39:23.720
Oh man.

00:39:24.260 --> 00:39:26.060
Uh, yeah. I don't know who wants to go first.

00:39:26.240 --> 00:39:27.120
Who's got thoughts?

00:39:27.340 --> 00:39:29.620
I mean, I got one.

00:39:29.840 --> 00:39:30.700
Okay, please.

00:39:31.180 --> 00:39:39.400
All right. So the game that I would remake, uh, on the PS5, um, and the Xbox Series X would be Lunar

00:39:39.400 --> 00:39:45.400
Pool. Now it's going to take some tweaking in terms of, uh, the scope, uh, obviously cause it's

00:39:45.400 --> 00:39:48.280
open world, uh, as well as like the, the lore.

00:39:48.500 --> 00:39:57.580
So basically Lunar Pool, uh, 2021 would be, uh, you live in a, a sort of, uh, a sort of

00:39:57.580 --> 00:39:59.820
cyber punky, like moon colony.

00:39:59.820 --> 00:40:03.000
Uh, that is, it's, it's industrialized.

00:40:03.200 --> 00:40:06.180
You, you have, uh, you have, you have little personal wealth.

00:40:06.420 --> 00:40:12.580
It's very corporate, but everywhere are these, uh, these, these pool halls that are seedy and

00:40:12.580 --> 00:40:14.560
they're, they're where the actual things happen.

00:40:14.560 --> 00:40:17.780
And you take on the role as a pool shark.

00:40:18.100 --> 00:40:23.020
And basically you, you would, you would go around this lunar city to the different, uh,

00:40:23.080 --> 00:40:27.740
pool halls. Uh, you would play pool, get into fights.

00:40:28.000 --> 00:40:33.120
Uh, there'd be some romance options, uh, of the bar flies at the pool hall.

00:40:33.120 --> 00:40:41.000
Um, and, uh, you, you'd eventually take down the CEO of this, uh, lunar corporation in a,

00:40:41.000 --> 00:40:42.140
a game of pool.

00:40:42.520 --> 00:40:46.100
You wouldn't like win anything, but you'd really show them who's boss.

00:40:46.260 --> 00:40:50.820
That's beautiful. I honestly, I think that, I honestly think that would be a fun, that'd be a fun game.

00:40:50.960 --> 00:40:52.900
You know, they, they, uh, I would play it.

00:40:53.020 --> 00:40:53.920
They gotta get quirky.

00:40:55.340 --> 00:40:56.840
Uh, Joe, do you have your choice?

00:40:57.040 --> 00:41:01.740
Yeah. I think what I, what I'm thinking, maybe maybe part of this is recency bias, but is spy versus

00:41:01.740 --> 00:41:07.920
spy. I think this is like, this could be the first ever exclusively two player open world game

00:41:07.920 --> 00:41:11.120
where you're both in the world together, setting traps worldwide.

00:41:11.500 --> 00:41:16.760
You're gathering fowlers and factions and just doing like Skyrim levels of things, but all

00:41:16.760 --> 00:41:20.780
just everything you're doing is like trying to go on a quest that'll just help screw over

00:41:20.780 --> 00:41:22.020
the other person in some way.

00:41:22.180 --> 00:41:24.500
So I think that, you know, you're always looking for where they are in the world.

00:41:24.700 --> 00:41:29.220
Joe, you're saying worldwide, but is it really like the entire world mapped out?

00:41:29.420 --> 00:41:30.780
No, it would be like a world.

00:41:30.920 --> 00:41:31.980
Our entire real world. Oh.

00:41:32.180 --> 00:41:33.260
Oh, okay. I see.

00:41:33.580 --> 00:41:35.460
Yeah. Like an entire real world.

00:41:35.600 --> 00:41:36.480
I got it. Yeah.

00:41:36.620 --> 00:41:38.200
To scale. Yeah.

00:41:38.500 --> 00:41:40.140
And you can go in any building.

00:41:40.580 --> 00:41:44.360
Yeah. Even like, yeah, even like the real people are all really there.

00:41:44.600 --> 00:41:47.820
No, even if it wasn't, you know, it could be, it could be any world, as long as it's large

00:41:47.820 --> 00:41:50.880
open world, the whole point of the game is to find and kill the other spy.

00:41:51.240 --> 00:41:53.140
Could take, could be an 80 hour game.

00:41:53.280 --> 00:41:54.280
It could be a 20 minute game.

00:41:54.920 --> 00:41:59.480
So do you have to set up like times that you play together.

00:41:59.840 --> 00:42:01.140
So do you have to set up times that you play together or can you play at any time?

00:42:01.500 --> 00:42:03.480
And you have to put your guy to sleep.

00:42:04.520 --> 00:42:05.820
Yeah. I like that.

00:42:05.920 --> 00:42:08.780
I was going to say you just have to keep playing until you're done or want to forfeit.

00:42:09.060 --> 00:42:10.540
But I like that idea better.

00:42:10.640 --> 00:42:15.920
Like you have to like find a good hiding spot to like, to like, to sleep while you're not

00:42:15.920 --> 00:42:18.760
playing. And then they could come kill you in your sleep.

00:42:18.900 --> 00:42:20.420
And then you turn the game on and say, well, you lost.

00:42:20.560 --> 00:42:22.240
You shouldn't have. I kind of like that.

00:42:22.440 --> 00:42:24.340
Yeah. And once you lose, that's it.

00:42:24.400 --> 00:42:25.800
Your copy can't work anymore.

00:42:26.260 --> 00:42:27.680
Yeah. Yep.

00:42:28.840 --> 00:42:33.440
Now, I'm going to give two answers here because I'm pretty sure I can't say my first one,

00:42:33.540 --> 00:42:35.080
which I was thinking of was Jaws.

00:42:35.680 --> 00:42:37.260
But that's not really a fresh IP.

00:42:38.020 --> 00:42:39.760
It's, you know, it's tied up in movies and everything.

00:42:39.760 --> 00:42:41.800
Oh, I guess neither is Spy vs. Spy if you put that right.

00:42:41.800 --> 00:42:42.920
Yeah. But you know what? It's fine.

00:42:43.280 --> 00:42:46.820
And I'm just saying like, to me, the Jaws game was already pretty close.

00:42:47.040 --> 00:42:51.480
Now, imagine that as an open world RPG where you're like trying to track down Jaws and you're

00:42:51.480 --> 00:42:55.620
you know, you're you're building out your ship and your your loadouts and you're getting

00:42:55.620 --> 00:42:56.760
stronger throughout the game.

00:42:56.760 --> 00:42:57.680
That would be great.

